          "explanation": "The change was about pharmacokinetics -- how the body handles a drug. Women eliminate zolpidem more slowly, so after the standard 10 mg dose, a larger share still had blood levels high enough to impair driving the next morning. Addiction is a real concern with sleep aids, which makes it a tempting answer, but it was not the reason for the sex-specific dose cut.",
