          "explanation": "Labeling a condition as belonging to one sex causes the other sex to be overlooked. Roughly 1 in 4 men over 50 will break a bone due to osteoporosis, yet men are screened and treated far less. The Yentl syndrome is a tempting pick, but Healy's point was specifically about women's heart disease; the broader lesson is that sex-blind thinking can miss risk in anyone.",
