          "explanation": "PCOS is linked to insulin resistance, prediabetes, type 2 diabetes, and cholesterol problems, so metabolic follow-up continues for life -- not just during fertility years. Endometriosis pain often does not track with how much disease is visible. The fertility-only answer is tempting because PCOS is often discovered during a fertility workup, but that framing is what leaves its metabolic risks unchecked. Both conditions are common, not rare.",
