          "explanation": "Being unable to urinate at all, with a painful distended bladder, is acute urinary retention -- an emergency that usually needs a catheter. Decongestants tighten the muscle at the bladder outlet and are a classic trigger in men with BPH. Drinking more water is the tempting wrong answer: it only fills an already over-full bladder. Saw palmetto has no proven effect even for routine symptoms.",
