          "explanation": "Women are more likely than men to have heart attacks with symptoms beyond classic chest pain -- shortness of breath, nausea, jaw or back pain, and unusual fatigue. Sudden onset of this cluster is an emergency. The tempting 'no chest pain, so wait' answer is exactly why women historically arrive at the hospital later. Calling 911 gets treatment started sooner; if it turns out to be something else, that is a good outcome, not a wasted trip.",
